  // SEQUENCE anti-leak (skill-harden 2026-09-14): safeproc/lockorder flash the whole answer at the START (arrow procedure / order-badged locks).
  // The material leak (answer in the descriptor) is closed by removing seq/order from `data`; here we additionally ONE-SHOT the frame (served
  // ~twice for a network/RAF retry, then locked) so the flash can't be re-pulled and OCR'd off-device after the show window. No time-gate is
  // needed since the flash is at t=0. If the frame render ever returns null the caller degrades gracefully (the input phase still runs).
